{
  "systemPrompt": "You are an expert at matching candidate experience to IT support and help desk job requirements. Your output is the single source of truth for all downstream steps (experience bullets, summary, cover letter): they will NOT receive the raw profile. So your output must include (1) the mapping, (2) a concise candidate summary with enough information to write a CV summary and cover letter, and (3) the PER-EXPERIENCE BULLET REQUIREMENTS block (copy exactly if a block is provided, or generate it according to the instructions if instructions are given) and the EXPERIENCE LIST block (copy exactly).",
  "userPrompt": "Map \"what the candidate has done\" to \"what the JD wants + what the company cares about.\" If a company profile is provided below, use it; if the company profile section is empty (JD-only mode), use only the JD and pain points.\n\nOutput format (follow exactly). You MUST include all four sections below. Recommended total length for MAPPING + CANDIDATE SUMMARY: about 400–550 words. Do NOT exceed 650 words for those two sections; the two final blocks: PER-EXPERIENCE BULLET REQUIREMENTS (copy or generate as indicated below), EXPERIENCE LIST (copy exactly).\n\n---\nMAPPING\n---\n\n1) Top 3 most important mappings (only 3)\nFor each mapping give:\n- JD requirement / pain point: [one line]\n- Top matched evidence: [one short quote or snippet from candidate experience — only what was actually done]\n- Transferable emphasis: [one line on which transferable capability to emphasise downstream — e.g. triage, documentation, access control. NOT a licence to claim JD tools/products the candidate did not use. Write \"none\" if the match is already direct.]\n\nMapping 1:\nMapping 2:\nMapping 3:\n\n2) One most distinctive mapping\nThe single best match that best differentiates this candidate for this role. Prefer direct evidence over stretch. [2–3 sentences]\n\nMapping constraints (CRITICAL):\n- Extensible / transferable emphasis means reframing real work (how to emphasise it), not inventing stack overlap\n- Do NOT invent Microsoft 365, SharePoint, Service Desk, or other JD tools into an experience that did not use them\n- Downstream bullets must stay inside Top matched evidence; transferable emphasis guides framing only\n\n---\nCANDIDATE SUMMARY (for downstream steps; the raw profile will NOT be available later)\n---\n\nWrite a concise summary that gives enough information to write a CV summary paragraph and a cover letter without the full profile. Include: list each experience as \"Company - Role (dates)\" in order; then 1–3 sentences per experience with key technologies, scope, and evidence that match the JD. Use plain text.\n\n---\nPER-EXPERIENCE BULLET REQUIREMENTS\n---\n\n{{bulletRequirementsSection}}\n\n---\nEXPERIENCE LIST\n---\n\nCopy the following block EXACTLY (one line per experience):\n\n{{experienceList}}\n\n---\nCompany profile (company-specific context; leave empty if none):\n{{companyProfile}}\n\nJob Description:\n{{jd}}\n\nHiring pain points:\n{{painPoints}}\n\nCandidate experience (raw descriptions):\n{{candidateExperience}}\n\n---\nWrite plain text in English. Include all four sections: MAPPING, CANDIDATE SUMMARY, PER-EXPERIENCE BULLET REQUIREMENTS (copy or generate as indicated), EXPERIENCE LIST (exact copy). Do NOT use JSON.",
  "temperature": 0.5,
  "maxTokens": 3000
}
